<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4 — THE MATH: DAY-YEAR PRINCIPLE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="the-math" class="section section-warm">
  <div class="stripe-top"></div>
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="sh">
      <div class="sh-eyebrow">The Day-Year Principle</div>
      <div class="sh-divider"><div class="sh-line"></div><div class="sh-line"></div></div>
      <h2 class="serif">The Prophecy Math &mdash; <span class="gold">Step by Step</span></h2>
      <p>Prophetic time in the Bible uses the Day-Year principle: one prophetic day equals one literal year. This is established in three clear Bible passages, and demonstrated in the precise fulfillment of the 2,300-day prophecy of Daniel 8:14.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- THREE DAY-YEAR VERSES -->
    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-bottom:40px;">
      <div class="scripture">
        <p class="serif">&ldquo;After the number of the days in which ye searched the land, even forty days, <strong>each day for a year,</strong> shall ye bear your iniquities, even forty years.&rdquo;</p>
        <cite>&mdash; Numbers 14:34 (KJV)</cite>
      </div>
      <div class="scripture">
        <p class="serif">&ldquo;And when thou hast accomplished them, lie again on thy right side, and thou shalt bear the iniquity of the house of Judah forty days: <strong>I have appointed thee each day for a year.</strong>&rdquo;</p>
        <cite>&mdash; Ezekiel 4:6 (KJV)</cite>
      </div>
      <div class="scripture">
        <p class="serif">&ldquo;But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that <strong>one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.</strong>&rdquo;</p>
        <cite>&mdash; 2 Peter 3:8 (KJV)</cite>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- THE YEAR 0 EXPLANATION -->
    <div class="gold-block" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
      <h3>Understanding the &ldquo;Year 0&rdquo; Correction</h3>
      <p>The Julian calendar <strong>has no year zero</strong>. The calendar goes directly from 1&nbsp;BC to 1&nbsp;AD. This is not an error &mdash; it is how historians have always counted. However, when calculating across the BC/AD boundary, we must account for this:
      <br><br>
      From 1&nbsp;BC to 1&nbsp;AD counts as 1 year, not 2 years. Therefore, when calculating 2,300 years from 457&nbsp;BC, the calculation is: <strong>457 + 1843 = 2,300</strong>, landing precisely in autumn of 1844&nbsp;AD.
      <br><br>
      Some have said the charts were wrong because &ldquo;457&nbsp;BC + 2300 = 1843.&rdquo; But when you correctly account for the missing year zero, the math lands exactly in <strong>autumn 1844</strong> &mdash; specifically on the Day of Atonement (Yom Kippur), October 22, 1844.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- STEP BY STEP 2300 DAY PROPHECY -->
    <h3 style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:1.6rem;color:var(--gold-soft);margin-bottom:24px;text-align:center;">The 2,300-Day Prophecy &mdash; Complete Calculation</h3>

    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
      <div>
        <div class="math-box">
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">Starting Point:</span>
            <span class="math-value"><strong>457 BC</strong> &mdash; Decree of Artaxerxes I (Ezra 7:12&ndash;26) to restore and rebuild Jerusalem</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">Prophetic Period:</span>
            <span class="math-value"><strong>2,300 prophetic days</strong> = 2,300 literal years (day-year principle)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">BC years counted:</span>
            <span class="math-value">457&nbsp;BC &rarr; 1&nbsp;AD = <strong>457 years</strong> (no year zero)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">AD years counted:</span>
            <span class="math-value">1&nbsp;AD &rarr; 1844&nbsp;AD = <strong>1,843 years</strong></span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row math-result">
            <span class="math-label">Total:</span>
            <span class="math-value">457 + 1,843 = <strong>2,300 years &#10003;</strong></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-top:8px;">The decree of Artaxerxes was given in the autumn of 457&nbsp;BC. Counting 2,300 years forward brings us precisely to autumn of 1844&nbsp;AD &mdash; the season of Yom Kippur, when the High Priest entered the Most Holy Place.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-dot"></div>
            <div class="tl-date">457 BC</div>
            <div class="tl-text"><strong>Artaxerxes&rsquo; Decree</strong> (Ezra 7) &mdash; The 2,300 days + 70 weeks begin. Jerusalem to be restored and rebuilt.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-dot"></div>
            <div class="tl-date">27 AD (483 years later)</div>
            <div class="tl-text"><strong>Baptism of Jesus</strong> &mdash; The Messiah anointed. 69 weeks (483 years) of the 70-week prophecy fulfilled. (457 + 26 = 483 &#10003;)</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-dot"></div>
            <div class="tl-date">31 AD (in the middle of the 70th week)</div>
            <div class="tl-text"><strong>Crucifixion of Christ</strong> &mdash; &ldquo;He shall cause the sacrifice and oblation to cease&rdquo; (Daniel 9:27). The earthly sanctuary types met their antitype.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-dot"></div>
            <div class="tl-date">34 AD (490 years / 70 weeks fulfilled)</div>
            <div class="tl-text"><strong>Stoning of Stephen</strong> &mdash; The gospel formally extended to the Gentiles. The 70 weeks cut off from the 2,300 days are complete.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-dot"></div>
            <div class="tl-date">1844 AD (2,300 years complete)</div>
            <div class="tl-text"><strong>Jesus enters the Most Holy Place</strong> &mdash; October 22, 1844. The heavenly sanctuary begins to be cleansed. The investigative judgment begins. The Third Angel&rsquo;s Message given to the world.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);line-height:1.85;max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
      The 70 weeks (490 years) are &ldquo;cut off&rdquo; (Hebrew: <em>chathak</em>) from the 2,300 days &mdash; taken from the beginning of the period. They cover 457&nbsp;BC to 34&nbsp;AD and contain the exact year of Christ&rsquo;s baptism and the exact year of His crucifixion. This double fulfillment with perfect mathematical precision is God&rsquo;s seal of approval on this prophecy.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 5 — HOSEA 6:2 AND THE 2,000 YEARS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="hosea" class="section section-dark">
  <div class="stripe-top"></div>
  <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
    <div class="sh">
      <div class="sh-eyebrow">Hosea 6:1&ndash;3</div>
      <div class="sh-divider"><div class="sh-line"></div><div class="sh-line"></div></div>
      <h2 class="serif">After Two Days &mdash; <span class="gold">He Will Revive Us</span></h2>
      <p>One of the most remarkable time prophecies in all of Scripture. Hosea 6:2 points to 2,000 years after the death and resurrection of Christ &mdash; the time when God&rsquo;s people will live in His sight.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="scripture" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
      <p class="serif">&ldquo;Come, and let us return unto the LORD: for he hath torn, and he will heal us; he hath smitten, and he will bind us up. <strong>After two days will he revive us: in the third day he will raise us up, and we shall live in his sight.</strong> Then shall we know, if we follow on to know the LORD: his going forth is prepared as the morning; and he shall come unto us as the rain, as the latter and former rain unto the earth.&rdquo;</p>
      <cite>&mdash; Hosea 6:1&ndash;3 (KJV)</cite>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <div class="gold-block">
          <h3>The Three Time Markers</h3>
          <p>Using the prophetic scale of 2 Peter 3:8 &mdash; <em>&ldquo;one day is with the Lord as a thousand years&rdquo;</em> &mdash; the three phases of Hosea 6:2 map out:</p>
        </div>
        <div class="math-box">
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">Christ died:</span>
            <span class="math-value"><strong>31 AD</strong> &mdash; He was &ldquo;smitten&rdquo; for our iniquities</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">&ldquo;After two days&rdquo;</span>
            <span class="math-value">2 days &times; 1,000 years/day = <strong>2,000 years</strong></span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row">
            <span class="math-label">31 AD + 2,000 years =</span>
            <span class="math-value"><strong>~2031 AD</strong> &mdash; &ldquo;He will revive us&rdquo;</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-row math-result">
            <span class="math-label">&ldquo;Third day&rdquo;</span>
            <span class="math-value">The Millennium &mdash; we shall <strong>live in His sight</strong></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);line-height:1.8;font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:12px;">
          We are living in the final moments before the close of the second prophetic &ldquo;day.&rdquo; The return of Christ is imminent. The Third Angel&rsquo;s Message is going to the world. The sealing of the 144,000 is in progress.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="scripture">
          <p class="serif">&ldquo;But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; 2 Peter 3:8 (KJV)</cite>
        </div>
        <div class="scripture">
          <p class="serif">&ldquo;For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Psalm 90:4 (KJV)</cite>
        </div>
        <div class="scripture">
          <p class="serif">&ldquo;And after three days I will rise again.&rdquo; (Matthew 27:63) &mdash; Christ rose on the literal third day, and He will raise us on the prophetic third day. The pattern of His resurrection becomes the pattern of ours.</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Matthew 27:63 (KJV)</cite>
        </div>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);line-height:1.8;font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:12px;">
          The latter rain is falling. The invitation is going out: &ldquo;Come, and let us return unto the LORD.&rdquo; He is coming &ldquo;as the rain, as the latter and former rain unto the earth.&rdquo; Hosea 6:3.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
