<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 6 — QUEEN ESTHER AND THE GOLDEN SCEPTER
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="golden-scepter" class="section section-warm">
  <div class="stripe-top"></div>
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="sh">
      <div class="sh-eyebrow">Esther 4&ndash;5 &mdash; The Royal Parallel</div>
      <div class="sh-divider"><div class="sh-line"></div><div class="sh-line"></div></div>
      <h2 class="serif">Queen Esther and the <span class="gold">Golden Scepter</span></h2>
      <p>The story of Queen Esther is one of the most beautiful prophetic pictures in all of Scripture. It mirrors exactly the experience of God&rsquo;s people in the last days &mdash; in the court of the heavenly King, with Jesus Christ as the Golden Scepter extended to all who approach in faith.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:36px;">
      <div>
        <div class="scripture">
          <p class="serif">&ldquo;Go, gather together all the Jews that are present in Shushan, and fast ye for me, and neither eat nor drink <strong>three days, night or day:</strong> I also and my maidens will fast likewise; and so will I go in unto the king, which is not according to the law: and if I perish, I perish.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Esther 4:16 (KJV)</cite>
        </div>
        <div class="scripture">
          <p class="serif">&ldquo;Now it came to pass <strong>on the third day,</strong> that Esther put on her royal apparel, and stood in the inner court of the king&rsquo;s house&hellip; and the king held out to Esther <strong>the golden sceptre</strong> that was in his hand. So Esther drew near, <strong>and touched the top of the sceptre.</strong>&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Esther 5:1&ndash;2 (KJV)</cite>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:16px;">
          After two full days of fasting&hellip; on the third day, Queen Esther put on her royal robes and entered the inner court before the king. The approach was forbidden by law &mdash; death was the sentence for any who entered without being summoned. But the king <em>extended the golden scepter</em> to her. She touched its top. And <strong>she lived in the king&rsquo;s sight.</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="gold-block">
          <h3>What Does This Mean for Us?</h3>
          <p>Esther fasted and prayed in total dependence and faith. She did not rely on her own righteousness. She put on royal apparel &mdash; clothed in dignity, not in her own righteousness</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="parallel-grid">
      <div class="parallel-col parallel-left">
        <h3><span>&#128212;</span> Queen Esther&rsquo;s Story</h3>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">1</div>
          <div class="pi-text">The people of God are under a <strong>death sentence</strong> &mdash; Haman&rsquo;s decree (Esther 3:13)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">2</div>
          <div class="pi-text">Esther <strong>fasts two days</strong>, submitting entirely in faith and prayer, with no confidence in self</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">3</div>
          <div class="pi-text">On <strong>the third day</strong> she puts on royal apparel &mdash; clothed in dignity, not in her own righteousness</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">4</div>
          <div class="pi-text">The king extends <strong>the golden scepter</strong> &mdash; the symbol of grace and acceptance and life</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">5</div>
          <div class="pi-text">Esther <strong>drew near and touched</strong> the top of the scepter &mdash; an act of faith and surrender</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">6</div>
          <div class="pi-text">She <strong>lived in the king&rsquo;s sight,</strong> and the death sentence against God&rsquo;s people was reversed</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="parallel-col parallel-right">
        <h3><span>&#10024;</span> The Last-Day Fulfillment</h3>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">1</div>
          <div class="pi-text">Every soul is under <strong>the sentence of death</strong> for sin &mdash; Romans 6:23, Revelation 13&rsquo;s death decree</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">2</div>
          <div class="pi-text">After <strong>two prophetic days</strong> (2,000 years), Hosea 6:2 says &ldquo;He will revive us&rdquo; &mdash; the time of revival is now</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">3</div>
          <div class="pi-text">On the <strong>third day</strong> (the Millennium) we will stand before the King, clothed in <strong>Christ&rsquo;s righteousness</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">4</div>
          <div class="pi-text"><strong>Jesus Christ is the Golden Scepter</strong> &mdash; God&rsquo;s grace extended to every human soul. He is our Mediator before the Father.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">5</div>
          <div class="pi-text">We <strong>reach out and touch the scepter</strong> by claiming and believing His Word &mdash; total dependence on Christ alone, nothing of ourselves</div>
        </div>
        <div class="parallel-item">
          <div class="pi-num">6</div>
          <div class="pi-text">We shall <strong>live in His sight</strong> &mdash; Hosea 6:2. The Second Death has no power over those who overcome by the blood of the Lamb and the word of their testimony (Rev. 20:6; 12:11)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:36px;">
      <div class="scripture" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;">
        <p class="serif">&ldquo;And they overcame him by <strong>the blood of the Lamb,</strong> and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death.&rdquo;</p>
        <cite>&mdash; Revelation 12:11 (KJV) &mdash; This is what it means to touch the golden scepter: complete reliance on the Word of God and total faith in the blood of Jesus.</cite>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

