<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 8 — FAQ
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="faq" class="section section-dark">
  <div class="stripe-top"></div>
  <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
    <div class="sh">
      <div class="sh-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <div class="sh-divider"><div class="sh-line"></div><div class="sh-line"></div></div>
      <h2 class="serif">Questions About the <span class="gold">Prophetic Charts</span></h2>
    </div>

    <div id="faq-list">

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Were the dates on the 1843 chart wrong?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>No. The dates were perfectly correct. The 2,300-day prophecy of Daniel 8:14 runs from 457&nbsp;BC (the decree of Artaxerxes) to the autumn of 1844&nbsp;AD. The chart used 1843 because that was the Jewish sacred year (spring 1843 to spring 1844), but the actual end of the prophetic period fell in autumn 1844 &mdash; specifically on October 22, the Day of Atonement.</p>
            <p>Ellen White wrote: <em>&ldquo;I saw that the 1843 chart was directed by the hand of the Lord, and that it should not be altered.&rdquo;</em> (Early Writings, p.74)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Why didn&rsquo;t Jesus return visibly on October 22, 1844?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>The Millerites misunderstood which sanctuary was to be &ldquo;cleansed&rdquo; (Daniel 8:14). They expected the cleansing of the earthly church or the return of Christ to earth. But the prophecy referred to the <strong>heavenly sanctuary</strong> &mdash; specifically, Jesus moving from the Holy Place (where He had been interceding since His ascension) into the Most Holy Place (the second apartment) to begin the final work of atonement before His return.</p>
            <p>The event was real and momentous &mdash; it just happened in heaven, not on earth. Hebrews 8:1-2 makes clear there is a true sanctuary in heaven that Jesus ministers in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          What is the significance of the Day of Atonement?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>In Israel&rsquo;s sanctuary service, Yom Kippur (the Day of Atonement) was the one day each year when the High Priest entered the Most Holy Place, before the Ark of the Covenant, to make final atonement for all of Israel. All Israel was required to <em>afflict their souls</em> (humble themselves, fast, search their hearts) on this day or be &ldquo;cut off&rdquo; from God&rsquo;s people.</p>
            <p>This ceremony was a type pointing to Christ&rsquo;s final work in the heavenly sanctuary in the end times &mdash; the antitypical Day of Atonement that began on October 22, 1844, and continues until the close of probation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          What does Habakkuk 2:2&ndash;3 have to do with the charts?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>God commanded Habakkuk that the vision would be written on tables so plainly that everyone who reads it can run with it. The Adventist pioneers understood this to refer to the prophetic charts &mdash; literally large poster-sized visual diagrams displayed in public meetings that presented the timeline of prophecy so clearly that any person could understand it at a glance.</p>
            <p>Ellen White specifically confirmed this connection: she saw that the charts were directed by the hand of the Lord and fulfilled the Habakkuk 2:2 command.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          What is the Third Angel&rsquo;s Message, and why does it connect to the charts?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>The Third Angel of Revelation 14:9-12 gives the most solemn warning in the Bible: those who worship the beast and receive his mark will receive the undiluted wrath of God and have no rest day or night. This message began with the opening of the Most Holy Place on October 22, 1844, and calls God&rsquo;s people to keep <em>&ldquo;the commandments of God and the faith of Jesus.&rdquo;</em></p>
            <p>The charts connected the time prophecy (pointing to 1844) with the content of that message: the heavenly sanctuary truth, the seventh-day Sabbath (the 4th commandment, the Seal of God), and the warning against the mark of the beast.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          How was the apostasy prophesied on the 1850 chart fulfilled?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>The 1850 Prophetic Chart warned that the final apostasy would be the formation of an "Image of the Papacy" — a Protestant church uniting with the state, copying Rome's structure, and enforcing religious authority through civil law. In 1904, under the presidency of <strong style="color:#fca5a5;"><a href="/april-15-1904-new-organization#signer-daniells" style="color:#fca5a5;text-decoration:underline;">Arthur G. Daniells</a></strong>, and in open defiance of the counsel of the Lord's messenger Ellen G. White, the General Conference leadership incorporated the church in Washington, D.C. as a civil corporation. The April 15, 1904 articles list the five signers who executed it: <a href="/pioneers/james-r-scott" style="color:#fcd34d;text-decoration:underline;">James R. Scott</a>, <a href="/pioneers/harvey-edson-rogers" style="color:#fcd34d;text-decoration:underline;">Harvey Edson Rogers</a>, <a href="/pioneers/daniel-k-nicola" style="color:#fcd34d;text-decoration:underline;">Daniel K. Nicola</a>, <a href="/april-15-1904-new-organization#signer-daniells" style="color:#fcd34d;text-decoration:underline;">Arthur G. Daniells</a>, and <a href="/pioneers/amos-p-needham" style="color:#fcd34d;text-decoration:underline;">Amos P. Needham</a>. <a href="/april-15-1904-new-organization#signers" style="color:#fcd34d;text-decoration:underline;">Meet the 5 Signers &rarr;</a></p>
            <p>The "Image of the Papacy" is not a statue — it is a system: a church that wields state power, enforces its will by law, and repeats the union of church and state that marked the Dark Ages. The prophecy is fulfilled.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          How does the year-zero correction work exactly?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>The BC/AD calendar system was invented by Dionysius Exiguus in the 6th century. It has no year zero: the sequence is &hellip;3&nbsp;BC, 2&nbsp;BC, 1&nbsp;BC, 1&nbsp;AD, 2&nbsp;AD, 3&nbsp;AD&hellip;. This means crossing from BC to AD only counts as one year, not two.</p>
            <p><strong>The calculation:</strong> From autumn 457&nbsp;BC to 1&nbsp;AD = 457 years. From 1&nbsp;AD to autumn 1844 = 1,843 years. Total = 457 + 1,843 = <strong>2,300 years exactly.</strong></p>
            <p>This is mathematically precise and arrives in the autumnal season of 1844 &mdash; the exact time of Yom Kippur.<br>
            <em>No correction needed. No fudging required. The prophecy lands exactly where God said it would.</em></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Can I download the original charts?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <div class="faq-inner">
            <p>Yes! Full PDF downloads are available on this page and on the individual chart pages. The PDFs include: the 1843 Prophetic Chart, the 1843 Chart Key of Explanation, the 1850 Prophetic Chart, the 1850 Chart Key of Explanation, the 1850 Law of God Chart (11&times;17 format), and the combined 1843 &amp; 1850 Charts PDF.</p>
            <p>These are high-quality historic charts and documents. They may be freely shared, printed, and distributed for the glory of God.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div><!-- end faq-list -->
  </div>
</section>

